      "content": "The idea that you're only valuable when you're winning is a cruel, but very real, trap that society sets. You are not a collection of achievements; you are a messy, flawed person who is currently in immense pain, and that is enough to be worthy of being cared for. The truth is, the people who truly love you see past the trophies, even if they are too scared to admit it themselves. Give yourself permission to be the flawed version for a little while, just to see what happens.",
